      "content": "When using an item for both business and personal purposes, the portion of its cost that you've used for business activities can generally be deducted as a business expense. Since you're primarily using the chair for work, you could allocate its cost based on how much time it's used for business versus personal activities. It's common to keep monthly or weekly logs to track your chair's usage separately for work and personal activities. As for tracking small expenses and receipts, you may consider using financial management software or apps designed to simplify your bookkeeping. These tools can scan itemized receipts, categorize them, and integrate them directly into your accounting software, making it easier to keep track of your finances and prepare for tax time. Once again, talking to a tax advisor will be immensely helpful to ensure you're following the best practices and legal guidelines.",
